  "problem": "What is the period of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{4x}{7}-{32}^{∘})?$",
  "worked_solution": "Given a function in the form $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=\\frac{4}{7}.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{{360}^{∘}}{(\\frac{4}{7})}={630}^{∘}.$",
